Subject: AOT: Layer A inline fast paths

What this does
  AOT: Layer A inline fast paths.

Why we need it
  Operand decode and site-index loads on every op.

What it adds
  Forty ROPs get a template that mirrors its interpreter handler one-for-one (property reads including the fused chain read, `put_field`, `get_element`, `get_local`/`put_local` and short forms, `get_arg`, `get_var_ref`, `load_this`, `move`/`move_s`/`move_xfer`, the `load_*` constants, `get_global`, the arithmetic and fused arithmetic ops, `binary_imm`, the branches and the generic binop/unop families); the engine exposes always-inlined `qjs_aot_*` fast-path helpers (`num_fast`, `unary_num_fast`, `own_read_hit`, `branch_cmp`, `set_reg_b/p`, `binary`, `arg_buf`, `put_local`, `get_global`, `put_field_own`, `get_element`, `get_var_ref`, `load_this`, `move_xfer`, `unary`, `to_bool`); the monolith entry fill consumes the backend's definite-assignment list `b->regvm_fill` (fill-all only when NULL) with the `AOT_MUT_FILL_DROP_ALL` negative control; `get_global` reads its atom from the live bytecode and `js_aot_gen_decode_insn` records each operand's byte offset.

Needs a bytecode version bump
  No.
diff --git a/quickjs-aot-gen.h b/quickjs-aot-gen.h
index 4eb64b7..bd60b05 100644
--- a/quickjs-aot-gen.h
+++ b/quickjs-aot-gen.h
@@ -54,4 +54,20 @@ void js_aot_gen_free(JSRuntime *rt, JSAotGenFunc *arr);
  */
 int js_aot_gen_insn_size(const uint8_t *code, int len, int off, int *p_op);
 
+/* One decoded register instruction for the template registry. `arg[i].kind`
+   is the format character, `val` the raw operand and `off` its byte offset in
+   the instruction (so a remapped atom can be re-read from live code). A
+   register's `val` is its byte offset in the register file; a branch target's
+   is relative to the END of the instruction. */
+typedef struct JSAotGenInsn {
+    int op;                 /* the ROP_* opcode */
+    int size;               /* total size in bytes, opcode included */
+    int nargs;              /* operands (<= 8 in the current ISA) */
+    struct { char kind; int64_t val; int off; } arg[8];
+} JSAotGenInsn;
+
+/* Decode one instruction into *out. Returns 0, or -1 under the conditions
+   js_aot_gen_insn_size refuses. */
+int js_aot_gen_decode_insn(const uint8_t *code, int len, int off, JSAotGenInsn *out);
+
 #endif /* QUICKJS_AOT_GEN_H */
